    {
      "_id": "ZOFBO9tYbSMLeUqk",
      "_key": "!journal.pages!YCxHPFDwwk4QiaET.ZOFBO9tYbSMLeUqk",
      "name": "Read Aloud",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<section class=\"sbn-leer\"><p>By day it smells of fish and flowers, and there are tourists taking pictures of everything. By night, the market is something else. The stalls are covered with tarps, the shutters pulled down, the red neon sign humming over an empty street. Below, on the lower levels, among corridors of closed comic book shops and stairways that lead down toward the bay, someone lights a candle.</p>\n</section>\n"
      },
      "sort": 200000,
      "ownership": {
